Mak3P $version | Windows x64 Full
=================================

Mak3P is a free, portable app for converting local audio and video files to MP3. It works offline on Windows 11 x64 and includes FFmpeg and ffprobe. No installation is required.

Get started
-----------
1. Choose Extract All in File Explorer and open the extracted Mak3P folder. Keep the bin and documents folders beside Mak3P.exe.
2. Double-click Mak3P.exe. Choose Add files to select files or folders, or drag them onto the window.
3. Choose a bitrate and Stereo, Mono, or Auto. The defaults are 320 kbps and Stereo. Under Output location, save beside each source or choose one writable folder for the entire batch.
4. Click Start conversion. Hover over a row or status for details. Cancel conversion stops unfinished work and keeps completed MP3s.

Mak3P supports FLAC, APE, WavPack, WAV, AIFF, AAC or ALAC in MP4/M4A, DSF, Ogg/Vorbis, Opus, WMA, AC-3, and MP3. It preserves supported tags and artwork. Hybrid WavPack conversion uses the .wv stream without applying .wvc correction files.

Source files stay intact. Existing output names receive numbered suffixes. Lower-bitrate sources use a supported bitrate at or below the target unless you enable Force upsampling. An MP3 that already matches the target can be skipped. Include MP3 from folders controls folder imports.

Help and licenses
-----------------
Open Mak3P > Help for the full guide. If bundled audio tools are unavailable, extract the entire ZIP again and keep both tools in bin.

Enable Write log file for a report beside Mak3P.exe. Review filenames, paths, and other personal information before sharing logs.

See LICENSES.txt for the Mak3P agreement and third-party notices. In the app, open Mak3P > About > License.

Report issues at https://github.com/Eager1Beaver/mak3p.
